WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.450
Lucía sees two sentences on
the board: Hablo español.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.930
Habló español.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.910
They look almost the same.

4
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.710
The only difference is a small
mark over the last letter.

5
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.550
The first one means "I speak Spanish.

6
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.810
" So what has that one
little mark changed?

7
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.470
In this mission, you'll
meet the preterite,

8
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.010
the past tense for finished actions.

9
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:26.630
It often comes with a time
word: ayer, "yesterday".

10
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.570
You'll build its endings
for the three verb families,

11
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.230
and find out which two
families share one set.

12
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.890
And you'll see why those
accents matter so much.

13
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.890
Your mission: work out what
one little mark can change.
